nload_url":"https://github.com/kenmaro3/ckks-train/releases/download/untagged-5876bf359b67f2d84117/SHA256SUMS"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kenmaro3/ckks-train/releases/assets/722420408","id":722420408,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVkh8-c4rD0K4","name":"source-inventory.json","label":"","uploader":{"login":"kenmaro3","id":35465898,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NDY1ODk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35465898?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3","html_url":"https://github.com/kenmaro3","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kenmaro3/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":1541258,"digest":"sha256:b3b1e108e778cd064586826f89d72587ea0a1f1eb24c12b6a4354104a394c7ec","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-08T00:42:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-08T00:42:55Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/kenmaro3/ckks-train/releases/download/untagged-5876bf359b67f2d84117/source-inventory.json"}],"tarball_url":null,"zipball_url":null,"body":"This is a research preview of ckks-train, an MIT-licensed Rust RNS-CKKS library for encrypted neural-network training. It includes the CPU non-interactive training path, CUDA arithmetic/evaluator implementation, archived measurements, and a ten-page single-author preprint by Kentaro Mihara.\n\nSource commit: `0b2d17a14cd305890d9eed771008d4f8617eff88`. Uncommitted Task54 work is excluded. The source archive has been read back and every tracked file and mode checked against Git. Asset hashes are in `SHA256SUMS`.\n\n### Evidence and limits\n\n- FULL-1 (196 inputs, B=64, one initial-weight seed) is archived. Its four key-switch ratios meet the registered numerical threshold. FULL-2 is still required for the registered comparison against ReBoot seed0 accuracy0.9041.\n- Full-setting official ReBoot CPU timing and the equal-security condition remain unresolved. GPU training/ablations and physical GPU bootstrap measurements remain unmeasured. This preview does not declare the original research plan complete.\n- Mac workspace tests:1,025 passed,19 ignored on00f4409; strict Clippy passed with and without CUDA. Subsequent code-path changes are a reviewed documentation link and notice wording. Strict rustdoc, formatting, license checks and archived table/figure regeneration passed oncf58897. Current Linux CI has not run because GitHub blocks runner startup for billing/limits.\n- The paper and arXiv source ZIP were built and visually checked locally. No arXiv submission or identifier exists yet. The paper is an interim preprint; its separate licensing notice is attached. Software remains MIT.\n\n### Reproduce the archived tables\n\nClone the repository, check out the source commit above, then run:\n\n```sh\nbash scripts/run_all.sh --tables-only\n```\n\nThis regenerates tables from archived evidence. It does not rerun the incomplete full experiment matrix. Git metadata is needed for provenance-producing experiment commands; a source archive alone does not provide it.\n\nRead `docs/research-preview.md`, `docs/m3-report.md`, `docs/m4-report.md`, and `docs/m5-report.md` for measured, unmet and unmeasured conditions. This is research code, not an audited deployment library.\n"}